+#version 120
+
+// Android GLES compatibility profile for ArenaMW complex PBR water.
+// Keep the complete PBR/refraction/foam/ripple lighting path, but avoid the
+// ArenaMW Android fast path for tiled GPUs / Sisah Openmw3 NG-GL4ES.
+// The old near-field path raymarched the water surface and evaluated FBM
+// height repeatedly per fragment. When water filled the screen this became
+// overwhelmingly fragment-bound. Keep the PBR/reflection/refraction pipeline,
+// but use the animated normal maps as the surface geometry source on Android.
+#define RAYMARCH_WAVES 0
+#define ANDROID_LITE_WAVES 1
+#define MOBILE_SURFACE_DETAIL 0
+
+// Shore foam toggle. 1 = foam on, 0 = foam off.
+// Foam also requires the engine's Wobbly Shores setting to be enabled.
+// The wobbly shore effect itself is always on (independent of this and of Wobbly Shores).
+#define FOAM_ENABLED 1
+
+// Set to 0 to disable distant water reflecting sky color instead of warping reflection UVs
+#define WATER_SKY_CONVERGENCE 1
+
+
+// Inspired by Blender GLSL Water by martinsh ( https://devlog-martinsh.blogspot.de/2012/07/waterundewater-shader-wip.html )
